{
  "example": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.ToolUsage.by_name`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.ToolUsage.calls`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.ToolUsage.result_bytes`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.ToolUsage.replay`\n\nAn agent invokes `read_node` twice, receiving 640 bytes of result text each time. A registered `lookup` tool returns the error text `absent`, and the provider request carrying that result is retried. The validator reports two calls and 1,280 result bytes for `read_node`, and one call and six result bytes for `lookup`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The example gives a concrete case with stated outcomes: `read_node` is invoked twice and returns 640 bytes each time. `lookup` returns the error `absent`. The provider request carrying those results is retried. The expected usage is 2 calls and 1,280 bytes for `read_node`, and 1 call and 6 bytes for `lookup`.\n\nThe test `tool_usage_counts_utf8_results_and_errors_once_across_retries` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` covers this scenario.\n- **Inputs:** the `Scenario` provider's first turn calls `read_node` twice and `lookup` with `{\"key\":\"missing\"}`. The second provider response is `Err(throttled())`, a 429 error that forces a retry of the request carrying those tool results. The third turn calls `submit_result`. The test runs `converse` with `MinimalConversation` and unwraps the result, so the retry must actually happen and succeed.\n- **Fixture behavior:** `MinimalConversation::dispatch` returns `\"λ\".repeat(320)` for `read_node`, which is 640 UTF-8 bytes (320 two-byte characters). It returns `Err(io::Error::other(\"absent\"))` for `lookup` with any key other than `value`, which is 6 bytes. So the 640-byte and 6-byte figures come from real multi-byte and error results.\n- **Assertions:** the test asserts the whole `tools` map from `domain.cache().usage().tools`. It expects `read_node` at 2 calls and 1280 bytes, `lookup` at 1 call and 6 bytes, and `submit_result` at 1 call and 0 bytes.\n\nThese assertions check each referenced requirement:\n- **`ToolUsage.by_name`:** the map has exactly the invoked tools as keys, including the built-in `submit_result`, with no extra entries.\n- **`ToolUsage.calls`:** the call counts are right, and the failing `lookup` is still counted once.\n- **`ToolUsage.result_bytes`:** the byte counts are UTF-8 lengths, 1280 rather than 640 characters. The error text counts as 6 bytes, and `submit_result`, which produces no result text, adds 0.\n- **`ToolUsage.replay`:** the retry after the throttled error leaves the counts unchanged. A double count on resend would give 4 calls and 2560 bytes for `read_node`, and 2 calls and 12 bytes for `lookup`. The exact-equality assertion would reject that.\n\nThe test carries `{test}` references to `usage_by_tool` and to the cited requirements. I found no unasserted outcome.",
